<title>CHILE: Codelco Andina supervisers sign 5-yr wage deal.</title>
<headline>Codelco Andina supervisers sign 5-yr wage deal.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Management and supervisors at Chile state copper company Codelco's Andina division have signed a five year wage contract, said the mine in a statement.</p>
<p>The pact, which comes into force August 1, gives supervisors a three percent increase in real terms in their basic salaries this year followed by a two percent increase in 1999.</p>
<p>Andina is the third largest of Codelco's four divisions. It produced 154,000 tonnes of fine copper last year.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
